WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Robocop, the future of law enforcement.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:27.060
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.080
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.320
And I'm Joe.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:36.160
And guys, it's worth saying I record that every single episode that and welcome to NEStalgia.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.140
I always do it the same way, but it has to be rerecorded every single time.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.760
It's not just a copy paste job.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.420
Yeah, we keep forgetting to save it.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.360
It's funny because I never hear you doing it again.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.560
So that's a little suspicious.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.000
Whoa, that's a problem with your headphones, buddy.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.920
It just can't pick up that word.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.860
Right. In fact, if listeners are listening to this episode and they don't hear anything, that's a problem with their headphones.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.020
You guys probably want to get those checked out because right now you're just listening to silence.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.940
If you plug in your headphones, you should hear us.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.600
Yeah, probably anytime you're listening to silence, the podcast is playing and there's something wrong with your headphones.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.560
Or if you're listening to silence, chances are you're not listening to the podcast, in which case you should be hitting play.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.000
True. Sean, what the hell are we here to talk about today?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:31.260
Well, there's a little something called Robocop and it's based off a movie also called Robocop from the 80s.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:43.320
It's an 80s movie, believe it or not, where there's a cop that's also a robot and he lives in Detroit and he raises a family.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.520
Okay, wait, but he wasn't always a robot.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.340
He kind of raises robot, half robot, half human family.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.000
It's sort of like Sims, an early Sims-like.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.160
I also might not have played the right game.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.860
Interesting. Okay.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:16.300
Well, I'll tell you that Robocop was kind of a, he was a cop, then he got like shot on the job, then they reanimated his lifeless body into a cyborg Robocop and that's how he becomes Robocop.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.480
Forget that his name was Lieutenant Alex Murphy.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.980
They just like, yeah, scrap the name.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.280
He's Robocop now.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.260
Like, oh, you know what? I did lost his name.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.860
I did play this game. Oh, very cool.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.040
Yeah. And if the movie wasn't enough, there were sequels to the movie and then a reboot of the movie.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.340
I saw a trailer for it that starred Samuel L.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:41.880
Jackson and just seemed kind of soulless, but that came out in like the 2010s, back when they were just remaking all these 80s action film stuff.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.360
And then there was a cartoon for kids too.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:50.100
And I don't think Robocop really lends itself to like animated kids cartoon Saturday morning stuff.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.140
Yeah, the movie's pretty violent.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.680
Yeah, it alludes to a misunderstanding of Robocop, I think.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.400
Sort of like Starship Troopers.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:08.040
Well, because I do remember before I knew really anything about the movie, I had this really cool Robocop toy that had like a lot of different like light up functions and, you know, like laser sounds and stuff.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.800
And like, that's how I knew Robocop was from this cool toy.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.140
And then I saw the movie when I was a little older.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.580
I was like, damn, this is a violent movie.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:23.240
It's funny that you mentioned that, Joe, because with a lot of movie video games that we've been getting, they've been pretty safe bets like Back to the Future and Who Framed Roger Rabbit.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.700
But we also got Rambo at one point.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.900
And that's a violent like movie as well.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:34.540
What else did we get? We got another like anti-war movie that got turned into a video game as well.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.300
It was I can't remember what that one was.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:44.440
But my point being that sometimes we get these games that don't really feel like they're for the market that was playing NES video games at the time.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.000
Robocop kind of bleeds into both territories.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:56.940
Like it's fine if you didn't see the movie because it's just a cool idea that this is a robot cop that you control like that works in video game form.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:03.280
I don't think kids needed to go see the presumably rated R movie to understand what was happening in the video game.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.080
They just maybe this was their only way to get access to Robocop.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:11.160
Yeah, but then it also like follows the plot beats for the most part.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:14.500
So that also is that.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.580
But like you, they're also not very, you don't really need to know what the plot beats mean.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:26.680
They're just like, oh, that's the scene from the movie, but it also could just be a scene in a video game.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:34.820
It's no different than the Spider-Man 2002 video game that came out a week before the movie and spoiled the entire movie.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.500
You managed to beat it in time.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.460
You actually watched the Green Goblin get killed by the glider.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.320
And it's like, oh, now you spoiled the movie for anyone who hasn't seen it.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:54.840
Well, I'll tell you one thing that I definitely didn't spoil the part that Spider-Man is not allowed to fall from the buildings because they're just clouds below them.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.320
Oh, yeah, right, right.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.540
Yeah, the buildings of New York City buildings are so tall that the clouds are below the buildings.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.620
But now I guess I've spoiled that part too, Joe.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.220
So you spoiled New York City.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.960
Yeah. Don't go on a trip to New York City.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.680
Now it's all spoiled. Bring it back to Robocop.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:21.200
I do think, though, that even if you were too young to have seen it, it was like, I feel like it was a big enough pop culture moment.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:31.520
And it was just like a part of the of like the pop culture of the day that like if you were a kid in the 80s, you were very aware of Robocop thought probably thought he was cool.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.700
And like if you hadn't seen it, you pretended you had seen it with your friends.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:40.360
So like it was probably still enough to get kids interested in the Robocop game.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.660
I'm guessing Robocop is kind of in the same way.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.480
GameCamp is the Terminator for me.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:51.800
And funny enough, they did wind up making like a game on the Sega Genesis Robocop versus the Terminator, which is interesting as well.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.180
Like Alien versus Predator.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.560
Yeah. They never made that movie, though.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.820
They should have made Robocop versus the Terminator.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.140
All this to say that, yeah, the movie doesn't really mean much to me.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.900
I grew up long after it and it's not really like in my cultural zeitgeist of things.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:25.760
So when I when I turned on the video game and everything, it was it was about what I expected for a Robocop movie video game, which is great because we've been getting a lot of movie video games that feel like they're really stretching out the idea of translating the movie into video game form.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:36.760
And Robocop just kind of gets it and makes it this action beat them up, run and gun crossover style game that just focuses on the violence of beating teenagers.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:40.120
It seems like there's a lot of teenagers that I'm kicking the crap out of.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.160
I don't I don't know if they're just way shorter.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.580
Yeah, I guess that's what's giving me the right.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:55.660
I never thought about how big Robocop might be that he's like potentially seven foot like like his legs extended from his regular sized legs.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:56.800
Like, did they make him taller?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:58.960
Not in the movie.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.580
Maybe in the video game.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.000
I think he is.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.200
He's taller.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:04.980
He's taller than human him.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.360
But I mean, it has been a long time since I've seen the movie.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:15.120
But what I going back to like this whole, oh, this is just a straight up video game version.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:24.760
It is refreshing that something that simple in something that I think at the beginning of this podcast would be like, oh, we're going to be really sick of this.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:34.920
I'm just like just make it a side scrolling action game like it doesn't need to be a capitalism simulator with with Ghostbusters.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:54.600
Or you need to learn how to navigate open waters in Jaws or even something as down to earth as Knight Rider where it's it's more so about just the driving things, which I which which is still probably what you wanted to play with Knight Rider.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.700
But it wasn't what the what the show was fully about.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.300
So, yeah, I was actually pleasantly surprised that it was this simple.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:16.580
And they make a choice to, you know, if I if I'm going to bring it close to Contra here, right, like they make it a choice to be both a beat them up with your your fists and close combat.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:21.420
And then in certain sections, you get to kind of use a gun.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.500
There are sections where you're not allowed to use a gun.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.600
That's not clear to me. So I'm not going to try to explain that.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.880
But basically, like sometimes you got to use your fists.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:30.740
And other times, I guess RoboCop deems it safe.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:31.860
Yeah, he just decides.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:33.680
Yeah. He decides for you.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.700
At first, I was like, oh, did I push a button that like unequipped my gun?

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:37.860
But no, it's just not.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.440
You're not allowed to use a gun in that space.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:53.020
So there is like this mix of both close combat action game and then this more Contra like run and gun style game where you can shoot in every direction, including diagonals, which is great.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.860
Always good to see a game that doesn't force you to just shoot up, down, left and right.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:04.200
But you do this in a world in which RoboCop, no matter how tall he is, cannot jump.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:09.480
Well, I think I was also thinking about this.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.780
I'm like, well, did we ever see RoboCop jump?

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.480
Like he's a big, heavy, like thing of metal.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:19.840
I don't know if I'm just if I'm giving them an out here or if that is sort of like canon.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.500
I kind of thought that about the whole way that he moves.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.180
He doesn't jump. He feels very heavy, moves very slowly.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:30.040
But in a way that seems like this like menacing.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:35.080
Yeah. Made of heavy metals, literally Terminator type character.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:40.160
Yeah, that kind of jokey walking like a robot, like as a joke.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:48.080
Yeah. But it felt right from what I remember the way that he moves in the movie.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:10:03.100
I don't know that making someone in this type of 2D side-scrolling game feel like he moves like RoboCop also translates to like fun movement.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:07.180
But it felt, it didn't feel out of place.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.920
Yeah, I think the combination of the no jumping-ness.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:23.280
Because whenever I think back to the movie, like I can hear like servos moving when he walks, but I don't know if that's just my brain playing tricks on me of what I should think to expect.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:40.100
But between that and the amount of punishment you can take from the enemies and just sort of the simplicity of his attack arsenal, whether it's guns or punches, it felt right.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:47.520
Yeah, it's not a bad design choice given that you're then forced to, you know, you can't skip over anything, right?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:56.020
But the problem becomes that the way that they design the levels is just a series of corridors and walking up or down stairs.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:03.480
There's no platforming whatsoever, but there's no inventive like navigation system at all.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:11.080
It's just walk from the left to the right and then, you know, here's a staircase, go up that staircase.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.440
Now go from right to left. You will have a lot of trouble navigating.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.960
Yeah. Yeah, the staircases in particular, they didn't really work out the kinks there.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:22.720
You have to be in the perfect spot for those staircases to walk up or down them.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.080
I think I had more trouble walking down them than up them for some reason.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.140
I also did, yes.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:35.300
Yeah, but it doesn't matter most of the time because as long as you clear the enemies off the screen, they don't respawn unless you also are moving.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.360
So it's fine.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:42.920
But there are some scenarios where it's very frustrating, where there's like a guy who it's like, they want you to go down the stairs and take care of him.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:46.060
But man, if I could just get down the stairs first, this wouldn't be a problem.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:56.520
It's so silly because even when, like after I was done playing and I was like, okay, now how does, what does it look like when somebody that really knows how to play this game plays this game?

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:04.800
And even like the no hit best run was like fumbling down the stairs.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:07.240
I'm like, okay, I feel related right now.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.620
I feel seen. Am I misremembering?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:16.100
I know that in Robocop, like one of the only things I remember is like the big bad robot in the end can't handle stairs.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:22.280
But does Robocop himself at one point have trouble going downstairs in the movie?

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.780
I like that we just keep canonizing faults.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:25.940
Yeah, I know.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:31.460
Like I'm not implying that I think that the developers did that on purpose.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.080
I just think it would be funny if that were the case.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:39.840
I vaguely remember that, but yeah, I don't think that it was an intentional design choice.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.300
I don't remember that.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:49.340
In the movie, were there also people who tried to attack Robocop but just conveniently jump kicked over his head?

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.320
Yes, most enemies.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.380
They would just jump kick over and they would just keep running.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:58.600
I thought that was funny that like most enemies are easily punishable, right?

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:08.480
There's not too many other than guys with guns at a distance point that it's like, oh, I kind of got to also line up and make sure my diagonal shot or whatever lines up with theirs.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.760
Most people that are charging at you in this game are meant to just, you know, one hit KO.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.380
Robocop is, you know, all invincible and super strong and all that.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:17.820
And that's fine.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.940
And that's fun. And it works from when you're supposed to feel like a badass.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.080
I think we were talking about this with Knight Rider.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:27.460
It's like, if Kit doesn't feel like the coolest car in video games, what's the point?

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.860
And, you know, with Robocop, I think they kind of embraced his overpoweredness.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:43.220
Maybe, I don't know, like the enemies themselves, though, could have been something more than just people that run up to you and try to punch you or people that jump kick over your heads.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:47.440
Or later on, it becomes machine weapons that shoot from a distance.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:54.060
Like, maybe they could have figured out something else to play with the idea that you can't jump, but other enemies can.

00:13:54.260 --> 00:14:00.540
It's kind of funny that the idea of that boils down to then them jumping over you and missing you completely.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:05.580
Now, do you think that Robocop should have been more of like a beat-em-up?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:13.060
Or, I'm not implying that's what you're saying, but do you think this was the correct genre for a Robocop game?

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:18.640
I do think it was the correct genre for a Robocop game, especially after having played Contra.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:27.560
Like, this feels like people who learned the right lessons from a successful video game and, you know, pretty much ripped it off and fit it onto the, skinned it onto the appropriate IP.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:36.240
And for the most part, whether this game is dynamic enough to be played in 2022, it played just fine for me.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:45.300
Like, I was playing through the levels, I felt good about both the player skill and the game difficulty to enjoy this game enough.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:54.600
I agree. I think that, you know, maybe even like the way that I'm talking about it, I'm not giving an accurate representation of how I felt about this game.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:15:00.880
I mean, I feel like the, on paper, I agree with everything you guys are both saying.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.640
I mean, I think this game played fine.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.920
I mean, it, you know, it, it made sense.

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:13.080
I just didn't really have much fun with the, like, with the, the, the movement, I guess.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:14.960
And like the, the gameplay loop.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:25.600
And it's hard for me to really put my finger on it because it's not that much different than like other kind of like side scroller beat them up ish games that we played like this.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:34.420
But it just, it just felt, even if it was intentional to make him slow and powerful feeling like that, just made it feel a little clunky to me.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.660
Like, like even.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.080
No, I totally get what you're saying.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.940
Even if I'm factoring in the fact that it was deliberate.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:44.060
You know, it just felt like, it felt like it was clunky.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.360
Enemies never presented too much of a challenge.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:16:00.840
So like the combination of like my movement, it, it, it felt a little bit more like I was, there were a lot of times where I felt like I had to like kind of work through a chore of just getting through really boring parts of the level to get to the next interesting thing.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.220
And then there'd be an interesting boss battle that was pretty fun.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:08.640
But like there was just a lot in between that felt like, like robotic.

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:18.640
Yeah. I mean, I think that this game, um, there's nothing really crazy in terms of like the gameplay and what you do.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:29.960
Like there's a cool, like fun moments where there'll be like a trap, a trap wall that you have to break a wall to get through to not get crushed.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:36.080
Or like there'll be new enemy types, like helicopters that you have to shoot from below.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:39.820
And there's that hostage situation that's kind of fun.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:42.900
They, they, they drew it out a little too long, but yeah.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:52.900
So there's little moments that, that break the monotony, but like what I liked about this game wasn't even so much how it felt to play or like the gameplay itself.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:17:05.240
I just, I think that if I can just move to like the visual presentation of this game for a bit, it's one of the coolest looking games that we've played on here.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:18.620
Uh, so far to me, uh, whereas in a lot of these side scroller games, a lot of the games seem to take place into just like random corridors that have, uh, just textures.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:23.060
This, this, like you're, you're, you're, you're walking through the city of Detroit.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:28.740
You're going through like a, uh, a factory or you're in a, an office building.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:43.860
And the thing that I liked about this stuff is between the detail and the backgrounds and the character sprites, it actually felt like a real place that you're side scrolling through instead of just a, uh, a textured path.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:49.520
So a lot of my enjoyment came from just the art of the game.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:53.340
Yeah. Even the, the RoboCop sprite is great.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:58.980
The, uh, cut scenes between levels are really, uh, cutting edge pixel art.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:03.460
Uh, maybe a little funny, uh, to some people nowadays, but I don't know.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:12.440
I thought it was, it was pretty gorgeous work, but I do agree with what you're saying, uh, Sean, but I did want to go back to what Joe was talking about with the, the movement.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.820
And I don't even think it's so much his speed or whatever.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:28.240
I think it's just the lack of movement options in this kind of game that make, that might make the gameplay feel more monotonous, not necessarily boring, but repetitive and just nothing really changes.

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:31.700
Yeah. We see, you know, new locate, new locations.

